{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work","id":978178,"title":"How does garou marriage/weddings work?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-28T21:04:34-07:00","id":978178,"title":"How does garou marriage/weddings work?","content":"So, a Female Fianna and a female Glasswalker want to get officially married...and i been thinking, how exactly does a wedding takes place between tribes?. i dont imagine them going to a human church.<br /> is there a &quot;Partnership ritual&quot;? or something? like an official one<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:32:22-07:00","id":978187,"title":"","content":"They do not because such relationships are against the Litany, even if they are homosexual relationships, because they are not supposed to form sexual relationships with other Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:32:33-07:00","id":978188,"title":"","content":"They would have to go to a particular and trusted sept of Black Furies and keep it secret, because the first tenet's interpretation can be a cruel weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:45:02-07:00","id":978196,"title":"","content":"And...what is one of the parts is actually sterile? would STILL be against the litany?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:02:44-07:00","id":978203,"title":"","content":"Short answer-yes.<br /> Long answer- Yes, but it depends on the Tribes involved in your scenario the Fianna are a very traditional tribe all of the material agrees on this. The Glasswalkers are the height of cutting edge so as long as you avoid some of the more conservative factions that might be a problem. However the Litany is quite clear Garou does not Mate with Garou the whole sterile argument is the justification for the claptrap that is the Children of Gaia Tribe Book. At the least I would expect the Fianna to be declared Ronin by the tribe perhaps the Tribe totem will disagree or another spirit may take up the cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:46:28-07:00","id":978229,"title":"","content":"Now, if a female Fianna Kinfolk and a female Glasswalker Garou decided to get married, there would probably be some flexibility after national legalization in 2015 in the USA, as long as both of them still reproduced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:48:33-07:00","id":978231,"title":"","content":"Such a relationship shouldn't be easy. For a Garou, life is conflict. If a Garou were to have a kinfolk mate, that includes a certain set of complications- and having a werewolf mate should be similarly thorny, if not moreso.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, these exact details can make for more compelling stories...<br /> <br /> Edit: I have said this before somewhere, but I am personally not a fan of Garou+Garou couplings, regardless of gender. Many parts of WtA are already spirit/fera centric, and without some human relationships to ground the Garou, it can be easy to lose sight of a big part of what fighting for Gaia even means. Having a kinfolk spouse and/or kids can really go a long way towards humanizing Garou characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 09-29-2016, 01:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:49:43-07:00","id":978232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978187#post978187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do not because such relationships are against the Litany, even if they are homosexual relationships, because they are not supposed to form sexual relationships with other Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Book of Auspices weighs in that this isn't as simple and straightforward as that. Some garou are against it sighting the Litany. Some Garou sight that it would count as a loophole because of the no metis deal. But much like say two metis coupling... I would imagine the vast majority of Garou would be publicly against it, but you could probably find some don't ask don't tell types around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:51:17-07:00","id":978233,"title":"","content":"As long as you agree to actually have babies with a kinfolk, it should be okay, but it is noted they place emphasis on monogamous marriages giving honor renown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T17:48:31-07:00","id":978740,"title":"","content":"Yes, but the Springtime rites of many tribes involve wild infidelity, which may be part of the point, that monogomous marriages are not &quot;What is expected&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd imagine when a garou and kinfolk marry, they first do a Human ceremony in the Tradition of the local culture.<br /> <br /> Fianna generally going for Irish Catholic, Silver Fangs Russian Orthodox... Stargazers buddhist, not sure on the rest.<br /> <br /> Then pay a brief courtesy visit to the sept with their spouse and introduce them as a gesture of politeness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:30:35-07:00","id":978761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978740#post978740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but the Springtime rites of many tribes involve wild infidelity, which may be part of the point, that monogomous marriages are not &quot;What is expected&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd imagine when a garou and kinfolk marry, they first do a Human ceremony in the Tradition of the local culture.<br /> <br /> Fianna generally going for Irish Catholic, Silver Fangs Russian Orthodox... Stargazers buddhist, not sure on the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>That assumption sounds like it's straight out of 1993.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T18:34:16-07:00","id":978763,"title":"","content":"Which one all 3?<br /> <br /> Assumption 1: The Garou having Springtime rites with wild Sex.<br /> <br /> Assumption 2: The Garou getting married in the Human world then paying a polite visit with their new spouse to the sept<br /> <br /> Assumption 3: The Fianna being Irish Catholic, Silver Fangs Russian Orthodox, and Stargazers Buddhist, thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 09-29-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T19:39:43-07:00","id":978793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978763#post978763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which one all 3?<br /> <br /> Assumption 1: The Garou having Springtime rites with wild Sex.<br /> <br /> Assumption 2: The Garou getting married in the Human world then paying a polite visit with their new spouse to the sept<br /> <br /> Assumption 3: The Fianna being Irish Catholic, Silver Fangs Russian Orthodox, and Stargazers Buddhist, thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Number three, though number one has seemingly fallen out of emphasis as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:07:04-07:00","id":978806,"title":"","content":"Well, why would they change in just 23 years? Though I would suggest that the Fianna would be just as likely to be Protestant as Catholic (especially in the USA), that Silver Fangs range across the religious spectrum, as they married into every royal family in Europe, and that the Stargazers would be just as likely to be Taoist as Buddhist (though religion is more of a thing for Kinfolk than Garou, as all Garou are supposed to worship Gaia as their primary). Just out of curiosity though, does anyone remember if there are any Mormon Garou or Garou Kinfolk mentioned in the books?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:13:19-07:00","id":978811,"title":"","content":"Think I saw a reference somewhere, and yes All garou are supposed to worship Gaia, had one player HATE that about the game, saying it took away her free will, blah blah blah blah blah blah blah blah<br /> <br /> Im afraid that the inherent mission is part of the APPEAL of the game, to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:23:26-07:00","id":978820,"title":"","content":"According to the All-Glorious Get (hallowed be they, May they rise to supremacy of the garou nation as the one true tribe) Essentially, Homosexuality is still breaking the spirit of the litany. A monogomous partnership that brings no children is even worse than a partnership that breeds a metis, because even a metis is more useful than nothing at all.<br /> <br /> An actual Female garou-Female garou wedding sounds more like a punishment rite than an actual rite in terms of mechanics and social acceptance. Such flagrant disregard for the litany is a high offense. You'd probably loose less being mother to a half dozen metis.<br /> <br /> Back from my ramblings. <br /> What you'd need them to do is to have the wedding done in mortal society, in secret. <br /> Later on, you introduce them to the shadow lords camp: The Judges of Doom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:39:33-07:00","id":978825,"title":"","content":"I Think the Judges only bother with blatant TREASON, not with this kind of superficial selfishness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:40:06-07:00","id":978826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978806#post978806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, why would they change in just 23 years?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, they would not have. You yourself observed this in the following:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Though I would suggest that the Fianna would be just as likely to be Protestant as Catholic (especially in the USA), that Silver Fangs range across the religious spectrum, as they married into every royal family in Europe, and that the Stargazers would be just as likely to be Taoist as Buddhist (though religion is more of a thing for Kinfolk than Garou, as all Garou are supposed to worship Gaia as their primary). Just out of curiosity though, does anyone remember if there are any Mormon Garou or Garou Kinfolk mentioned in the books? </div> </div> </div>Textually speaking, there isn't a change. Just better research going into the metatext, with fewer broad brushes. Sometimes, though, we have backsliding, such as W20 over-emphasizing alleged Russian roots in the Fangs, for instance, when the first tribebook had them spread out through North Africa and most of the rest of Asia as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Think I saw a reference somewhere, and yes All garou are supposed to worship Gaia, had one player HATE that about the game, saying it took away her free will, blah blah blah blah blah blah blah blah</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Im afraid that the inherent mission is part of the APPEAL of the game, to me.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;All Garou are spiritual. Not all Garou are religious.&quot;<br /> <br /> They do not worship Gaia, as such. They are <i>devoted</i> to her, in a manner not entirely unlike the protagonist of Yandere Simulator being of a &quot;devoted&quot; personality type (one of the key differences being that Garou and Fera, other than Ananasi, usually feel a whole hell of a lot, a far cry from hollow emptiness).</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 09-29-2016, 11:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T20:40:23-07:00","id":978827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978793#post978793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Number three, though number one has seemingly fallen out of emphasis as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Rite of the Birth Season was printed in Book of the Wyld, in 3rd edition so you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T21:06:51-07:00","id":978834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978827#post978827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Rite of the Birth Season was printed in Book of the Wyld, in 3rd edition so you know.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it's appeared before. It's also not really well-emphasized in writing on Garou culture. The ramifications of it are touched on where it's written and nowhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T21:35:26-07:00","id":978845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978826#post978826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically, they would not have. You yourself observed this in the following:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Textually speaking, there isn't a change. Just better research going into the metatext, with fewer broad brushes. Sometimes, though, we have backsliding, such as W20 over-emphasizing alleged Russian roots in the Fangs, for instance, when the first tribebook had them spread out through North Africa and most of the rest of Asia as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot;All Garou are spiritual. Not all Garou are religious.&quot;<br /> <br /> They do not worship Gaia, as such. They are <i>devoted</i> to her, in a manner not entirely unlike the protagonist of Yandere Simulator being of a &quot;devoted&quot; personality type (one of the key differences being that Garou and Fera, other than Ananasi, usually feel a whole hell of a lot, a far cry from hollow emptiness).</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Mom, Dad. Please stop fighting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:26:08-07:00","id":978863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978845#post978845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mom, Dad. Please stop fighting</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd know fighting. This is still pretty civil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T22:43:35-07:00","id":978870,"title":"","content":"Well, this is like &quot;Opposites Attract&quot;, right? Because on one hand you have one of the most literal, conservative, fanatical Tribes, and the other is one of the most liberal, non-traditional, open-minded Tribes... so one side's family is going to bring their klaives and try to gut the fiance.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, Fianna are going to say &quot;Thou shall not mate, marry, or wed another Garou, even if it's same-sex. And same-sex is against tradition, so that ain't gonna happen under our watch, lass.&quot;<br /> It's probably better if the Fianna goes through Rite of Renunciation and tries to join the Glass Walkers (if Cockroach will accept her.) The Glass Walkers are a bit more forgiving and forward-thinking. They're still not cool on metis, but this pairing isn't going to make any, so I don't see the 'Walkers having that big of a deal with it... other than getting grief from local purists in the Sept/region.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason my characters often bring up when concerning the 1st Law is that Garou who are concerned about their loved ones also on the battle field open themselves up to being manipulated and not being of sound mind when it comes to war. Keeping your mate/children away from the daily life of being a Warrior, and especially off of the battlefield keeps their two worlds separated. Therefore, the law not only keeps the two from making Metis (traditionally), but works to keep Garou paired with Kin who they can leave behind to care for their children and out of the immediate war... at least on the scale that the Garou do in most cases.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T00:08:50-07:00","id":978898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978825#post978825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Think the Judges only bother with blatant TREASON, not with this kind of superficial selfishness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope. It's a flagrant disregard for the litany. The kinda stuff that encourages others to sin should it go unpunished. The kind of shit that gets judges all riled up in their wee judgy booties. The kind that makes them put on disco music before they spin the dagger. They're coming for you, and they'll kill you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T02:33:35-07:00","id":978933,"title":"","content":"The Judges don't care if you have a gay relationship so long as you produce children with Kinfolk as that's a Duty and so long as no metis are produced. The Shadowlords tribe has a big history of this kind of behaviour and also being very Understanding to Garou of other tribes who find themselves having these issues. It's one of their manipulation power bases. <br /> <br /> As for marriages. It varies massively from Tribe to Tribe and Sept to Sept even but in most cases there is a Rite involved, often one of the fertility Rites as Garou and Kinfolk don't tend to get Wed as such, they become Mated, they take a Mate (or Mates for that matter). The institutionalised wedding process of the mortal world (especially through the major religious structures) is something you're not overly likely to see. For one they're not spiritually gnostic Gaia centric and two imagine the stresses of a normal wedding planning and ceremony, now add in Rage, bound to end badly. What you'll see more of instead are the 'pagan' tribal cultural roots echoed, which were typically a lot more relaxed affairs (or with better options in their structuring for Rage monsters to not explode). Again it varies from Tribe to Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T05:31:08-07:00","id":978960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978898#post978898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Nope. It's a flagrant disregard for the litany. The kinda stuff that encourages others to sin should it go unpunished. The kind of shit that gets judges all riled up in their wee judgy booties. The kind that makes them put on disco music before they spin the dagger. They're coming for you, and they'll kill you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think your right sorry but judges would probaly in most Cases leave Charachs to the local Truth Catcher<br /> <br /> Unless the sept seems to be turning a blind eye to them...<br /> <br /> in which case the whole SEPT needs an inquisition...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T06:29:40-07:00","id":978977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978811#post978811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think I saw a reference somewhere, and yes All garou are supposed to worship Gaia, had one player HATE that about the game, saying it took away her free will, blah blah blah blah blah blah blah blah<br /> <br /> Im afraid that the inherent mission is part of the APPEAL of the game, to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'll need a page reference for that. &quot;Revere&quot;, maybe, but not &quot;Worship&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:06:59-07:00","id":978995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978870#post978870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is like &quot;Opposites Attract&quot;, right? Because on one hand you have one of the most literal, conservative, fanatical Tribes, and the other is one of the most liberal, non-traditional, open-minded Tribes... so one side's family is going to bring their klaives and try to gut the fiance.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, Fianna are going to say &quot;Thou shall not mate, marry, or wed another Garou, even if it's same-sex. And same-sex is against tradition, so that ain't gonna happen under our watch, lass.&quot;<br /> It's probably better if the Fianna goes through Rite of Renunciation and tries to join the Glass Walkers (if Cockroach will accept her.) The Glass Walkers are a bit more forgiving and forward-thinking. They're still not cool on metis, but this pairing isn't going to make any, so I don't see the 'Walkers having that big of a deal with it... other than getting grief from local purists in the Sept/region.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of assumptions are always flawed same with the judges of Doom, many people seem to think the group in WoD as infalible entities devoid of context and agendas.<br /> <br /> Would the Fianna ask the female garou to renounce their tribe? Depends, is the sept full of elders &quot;set-in-their-ways&quot; that oppose this? Or is the female garou one of the big ranks on the sept and thus could kick the asses of the fiana back in place? Or the place is so devoid of fianna that removing another one is killing the tribe on the sept.<br /> <br /> How is the balance of power in the sept? Is feasible for them to pull a red wedding? Do they want to? Maybe the female garou grease the gears of the elder fianna in the sept to back her up. For example she could have accepted to mate with fianna kin a set number of times and give the offspring to the elder and thus strenghtening the elder political position.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the glass walker surpass the fianna 3 to 1 so pulling a klaive red wedding on them is akin to result in lots of fianna corpses and new klaives to the glasswalkers.<br /> <br /> Same with the judges of doom, would they care about something like that? Or declare something like a &quot;Sept inquisition&quot;? Because that seems incredible bad political move and just result in more effort than its worth and assumes that a) The offending garous arent making any consetions and B) The judge dont have anything better to do, no pressing matters or more pressing violations. And C) They can actually pull it off or they would get their asses kick and loss more judges than its worth.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for wedding i have played games where a Shadowlord marriage was done in classic russian custom on the sept and a marriage between 2 (kin and garou) Silver Fangs was done by the silver fang declaring on the moot on the announcement part &quot;Oh and, Johny and me are mated now. He is mine, i lick him first and if any of you touch them i rip your throats&quot;. But something i have use is a Silver Fang rite, i think from their revised tribebook in which the participant exchange a gift and promise something as way of wedding. I think its name &quot;Rite of the honorable oath&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T07:58:23-07:00","id":979018,"title":"","content":"I am not quite sure if many Tribes (with the possible exceptons of the Silver Fangs or Wendigo) really care about marriage right now. They are rare, something like 15,000 globally, so they are probably focused on reproduction over relationships. Garou are probably being encouraged to have lots of unprotected sex, to maximize the probability of pregnancy, since they do not have to worry about disease.<br /> <br /> Since average human fertility gives a 2.5% of pregnancy from each unprotected sexual act, Garou need to have a fair amount of sex to get a child. In the USA, around 75% of unattached females are on birth contro. Of those not of birth control, 75% will have an abortion over an unwanted child.<br /> <br /> Because female Garou are not on birth control and want any resulting child, they are 16 times more likely to end up with a child from an unprotected sexual act than a male Garou, but they have to be willing to breed. Garou society would probably see a lesbian marriage as a sign of reduced willingness of both partners to reproduce. I think they would at least need to select a couple of male Kinfolk to help them reproduce before they would be accepted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T17:42:41-07:00","id":981130,"title":"","content":"Well... when two garou love each other veeeeery much the ritemaster will host a big and wonderful ceremony at the local moot.<br /> <br /> Both garou will walk down a long isle to the front of an alter to Gaia. Galliards and ragabash will be shouting and singing and when you get there, the ritemaster spits on you, brands you with burning iron and then the rest of the garou can viciously beat the shit out of you for being a filfthy litany breaking little shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","user":"Cantankerous Bees","date":". 10-03-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T18:46:26-07:00","id":981174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=978995#post978995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This kind of assumptions are always flawed same with the judges of Doom, many people seem to think the group in WoD as infalible entities devoid of context and agendas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're kinda forgetting that A lot of Garou are fanatical. Even Shadow lords do their perceived duty to Gaia more often than they do all the backstabbing politicking they're famous for. I'm not entirely sure about the ratio, but there's going to be Judges who use cunning and threats to get what they want, and there's going to be hardliners that wreck anyone who makes a serious transgression. Judges of doom will come from all auspices (and I think they work in twos. Do they work in twos or am I just remembering stuff wrong and not looking back onto it because I'm lazy) and just as they come from different auspices, different strategies will be used in aproaching issues (even though we're all probably imagining a load of philidox) <br /> Of course, the group is going to be selective about the matter, and I imagine abuses of power will be subject to the harshest of punishments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:12:10-07:00","id":981197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/978178-how-does-garou-marriage-weddings-work?p=981174#post981174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're kinda forgetting that A lot of Garou are fanatical. Even Shadow lords do their perceived duty to Gaia more often than they do all the backstabbing politicking they're famous for. I'm not entirely sure about the ratio, but there's going to be Judges who use cunning and threats to get what they want, and there's going to be hardliners that wreck anyone who makes a serious transgression. Judges of doom will come from all auspices (and I think they work in twos. Do they work in twos or am I just remembering stuff wrong and not looking back onto it because I'm lazy) and just as they come from different auspices, different strategies will be used in aproaching issues (even though we're all probably imagining a load of philidox) <br /> Of course, the group is going to be selective about the matter, and I imagine abuses of power will be subject to the harshest of punishments.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't come from different auspices if I remember the tribebook correctly. They're an all philadox faction (sorta like how the SF Ivory Priests are all Theurge)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:40:01-07:00","id":981437,"title":"","content":"I used to think of them as all philodex, but more recent Material changed that.